WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:03.773
Line 3 in hall B gets a heavier connection.

2
00:00:04.508 --> 00:00:06.470
That is work for the grid operator.

3
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:12.378
A grid operator connects customers, maintains the grid and restores outages,

4
00:00:12.541 --> 00:00:13.447
day and night.

5
00:00:14.507 --> 00:00:16.016
Four topics follow the job.

6
00:00:16.735 --> 00:00:18.999
First the request and the field work.

7
00:00:20.096 --> 00:00:23.103
Then the daily work with outages and a full grid.

8
00:00:24.442 --> 00:00:27.054
The first topic is From request to connection.

9
00:00:27.751 --> 00:00:29.748
The plant applies and gets an offer.

10
00:00:30.842 --> 00:00:34.708
Then comes work preparation with permit, material and planning.

11
00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:37.262
The work preparer arranges it.

12
00:00:38.294 --> 00:00:42.079
The work preparer runs a readiness check before the job starts.

13
00:00:42.756 --> 00:00:44.683
So the crew does not come for nothing.

14
00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:47.945
The second topic is Field work.

15
00:00:48.726 --> 00:00:51.721
A heavier cable to hall B is work for the crew.

16
00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:55.268
For that the crew switches a part of the grid off,

17
00:00:55.373 --> 00:00:57.741
makes it safe and switches it back on.

18
00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:00.835
The wrong order can drop customers.

19
00:01:01.858 --> 00:01:05.481
The technician switches by a switching plan, step by step.

20
00:01:06.218 --> 00:01:07.669
So the crew works safely.

21
00:01:08.951 --> 00:01:11.830
The third topic is Outages and asset risk.

22
00:01:12.558 --> 00:01:15.635
If a cable fails, the plant can be without power.

23
00:01:16.668 --> 00:01:19.571
The control room watches the grid day and night.

24
00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:22.285
It sees a trip within seconds.

25
00:01:23.297 --> 00:01:25.816
The technician reads the fault indicators.

26
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.295
So he sees which piece of cable is broken.

27
00:01:30.379 --> 00:01:33.235
Then the centre closes the normally open point.

28
00:01:33.986 --> 00:01:35.658
So the plant has power again.

29
00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:40.326
The fourth topic is Congestion management in operations.

30
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.080
At peak moments the grid is full.

31
00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:48.317
A team next to the centre steers offtake and feed-in at those moments,

32
00:01:48.445 --> 00:01:50.720
so more customers fit on a full grid.

33
00:01:51.738 --> 00:01:54.130
It buys flexibility through GOPACS.

34
00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:59.107
So the grid keeps running while line 3 gets its heavier connection.

35
00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:01.230
The whole map.

36
00:02:01.942 --> 00:02:06.447
Grid operations and assets is the sixth station of Energy and the grid.

37
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.210
Every topic has four levels.

38
00:02:10.206 --> 00:02:13.120
Start with Requesting a connection at Basics level.

39
00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.571
That lesson shows the way from request to offer.

40
00:02:17.594 --> 00:02:19.800
At Working knowledge level come commissioning,

41
00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.329
safe switching, the fault service and the congestion study.

42
00:02:24.328 --> 00:02:27.707
At Advanced level come asset data and grid models,

43
00:02:27.927 --> 00:02:31.398
crew planning, asset management and the congestion desk.

44
00:02:32.457 --> 00:02:35.069
At Expert level it is about honest dates,

45
00:02:35.232 --> 00:02:39.168
wrench time, learning from outages and flexibility or waiting.

46
00:02:40.204 --> 00:02:44.384
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
